-- title:
--   Base-point-free section of 𝒪(mε) on a K-fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $c \colon C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $\varepsilon$ consist of a morphism $\varepsilon_1 \colon \operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ together with the identity $\varepsilon_1 \circ$-relation $\varepsilon_1 \gg c = \mathbb 1$, i.e. a section of $c$. Let $g$ be a natural number subject to the hypothesis that for every algebraically closed field $k$, every $s \colon \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, every field extension $L/k$, every `CurveModel` $M$ for $L/k$ (an integral scheme $M.C$, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, with function field identified with $L$ over $k$, closed points in bijection with the places of $L/k$ matching stalks to valuation rings, and every finite set of points contained in an affine open) together with an isomorphism $e \colon M.C \cong C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} k$ compatible with the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} k$, every divisor $K_c$ of $L/k$ and every $g'$: if $\ell(D) - \ell(K_c - D) = \deg D + 1 - g'$ for all divisors $D$ (with $\ell$ the $k$-dimension of the Riemann–Roch space), then $g' = g$. Let $m$ satisfy $2g \le m$ and $1 \le m$, let $\mathcal V$ be a cover of $C$ by two affine opens $U_0, U_1$ with $U_0 \sqcup U_1 = C$ and $U_0 \cap U_1$ affine, and let $K$ be a field that is an $R$-algebra. Write $C_K = C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} K$ and let $\mathcal I = \ker \varepsilon_1$ be the ideal sheaf of the section. Then there is a morphism of modules $s$ on $C_K$ from the unit object (the structure sheaf) to the pullback along the first projection of $(\mathcal I^m)^\vee$, the dual of the module attached to $\mathcal I^m$, such that for every $z \colon \operatorname{Spec} K \to C_K$ with $z$ followed by the first projection equal to $\varepsilon_1 \circ \operatorname{Spec}(R \to K)$ and $z$ followed by the second projection the identity, the image under $z$ of the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} K$ does not lie in the support of the ideal sheaf $\mathcal Z(s)$, the infimum of all ideal sheaf data whose ideal on each affine open contains the ideal generated by the coefficients of $s$ there.
--
--   This is the statement that on the fibre over $K$ of a pointed smooth proper curve of genus $g$ the complete linear system $|m\varepsilon|$ has no base point at the marked section, once $m \ge \max(2g,1)$; the section is produced as a global section of the pullback of $\mathcal O(m\varepsilon) = (\mathcal I^m)^\vee$ whose zero scheme avoids the marked point. It feeds the constructions [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_forall_le_exists_section_invModule_disjoint_of_twoAffineOpenCover`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_forall_le_exists_section_invModule_disjoint_of_twoAffineOpenCover), [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_section_invModule_pow_ker_disjoint`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_section_invModule_pow_ker_disjoint) and [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_section_invModule_pow_ker_notMem_support_of_isMaximal`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_section_invModule_pow_ker_notMem_support_of_isMaximal) in the relative Picard and Néron model infrastructure.
